# Claude Code — Avista house rules

The rules that apply to everyone at Avista live in the avista-docs repo
(https://github.com/Avista/avista-docs, `engineering/standards/`) and are imported below.
`~/.claude/avista-docs` is the clone, or a link to it. Change a rule with a pull request there, not here.
Run `git -C ~/.claude/avista-docs pull` to pick up merged changes.

If `~/.claude/avista-docs` is missing, these imports load nothing and the house rules are silently
absent. `dev-machine-doctor` checks for it.

@~/.claude/avista-docs/engineering/standards/working-with-claude.md
@~/.claude/avista-docs/engineering/standards/git.md
@~/.claude/avista-docs/engineering/standards/coding-style.md
@~/.claude/avista-docs/engineering/standards/wordpress-plugins-and-themes.md
@~/.claude/avista-docs/engineering/standards/secrets.md
@~/.claude/avista-docs/engineering/standards/metered-apis.md
